Subject: [PATCH] allow several restriction enzymes in --cutter

wf-pore-c passes --cutter straight to `pore-c-py digest`, which accepts a
single enzyme. Protocols using two or more (DpnII + NlaIII, or Arima's
DpnII + HinfI) therefore have the junctions of the second enzyme left
undigested: the affected monomer spans two loci, aligns to one, and the rest
is soft-clipped away.

This swaps the digest for `pore-c-aqb digest`, which takes a comma-separated
list and cuts at the union of the sites, and relaxes the schema so a list is
accepted. With a single enzyme the output is byte-identical to before.

Requires pore-c-aqb in the process container:
    pip install git+https://github.com/AQB/wf-pore-c_AQB.git

---
 modules/local/pore-c.nf | 2 +-
 nextflow_schema.json    | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/local/pore-c.nf b/modules/local/pore-c.nf
--- a/modules/local/pore-c.nf
+++ b/modules/local/pore-c.nf
@@
-    pore-c-py digest "${params.cutter}" --max_monomers ${params.max_monomers} \
+    pore-c-aqb digest "${params.cutter}" --max_monomers ${params.max_monomers} \
         --excluded_list "filtered_reads.txt" \
         --header "concatemers.bam" \
         --threads ${task.cpus} |

diff --git a/nextflow_schema.json b/nextflow_schema.json
--- a/nextflow_schema.json
+++ b/nextflow_schema.json
@@
             "cutter": {
                 "type": "string",
-                "description": "The enzyme used in the restriction digest.",
-                "help_text": "Any enzyme from the Biopython restriction dictionary can be used.",
+                "description": "The enzyme(s) used in the restriction digest.",
+                "help_text": "Any enzyme from the Biopython restriction dictionary. Several may be given, comma-separated, e.g. 'DpnII,NlaIII' - cut points are the union of their sites.",
                 "default": "DpnII"
             },
